 "scribe_vocals_2": {
  "text": "Motion, motion. Change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe. Motion, motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run. Sleeping, air moves into and out of our lung. Blood flows in arteries and veins. Carried people, automobiles and planes. Water flowing down a dam. Leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every twenty-four hours. Revolves round the sun once in a year. The sun in motion in the Milky Way, Milky Way. Moving within its local group of galaxies. Hey. Rectilinear motion. Uniform acceleration. A set of simple equations. Relative nature of motion. Relative velocity. Point objects. Valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life. Good number of situations. Size neglected without much error. Motion, motion. Change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line.",
